# Pins and releases

Three sibling repos: `lobbs` (plugin), `lobbs-meshtastic-firmware`, `lobbs-meshcore-firmware`. Each fork pins the plugin through `lib_deps`. The Meshtastic fork enables LoBBS on every env.

## Local dev: symlink, never committed

Point a fork at the working copy with a gitignored override:

| Fork | Override file | Content |
| --- | --- | --- |
| MeshCore | `platformio.local.ini` (already gitignored, already in `extra_configs`) | `lib_deps` with `lobbs=symlink://../lobbs` |
| Meshtastic | `lobbs.local.ini` (gitignored, loaded last via `platformio.ini` `extra_configs`) | same |

- `symlink://` never appears in a committed file. A pushed symlink breaks MeshForge and CI, because the path only exists locally.
- Before pushing a fork, `git grep -n 'symlink://'` on overlay ini files must return nothing.

## Committed pin

```ini
lobbs=https://github.com/MeshEnvy/lobbs.git#<full 40-char plugin commit sha>
```

Pin by commit, not branch. A commit pin is immutable, and PlatformIO fetches it without a recursive clone.

## Tags

| Repo | Format | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lobbs` | `vX.Y.Z` | `v2.1.0` |
| `lobbs-meshtastic-firmware` | `lobbs-vX.Y.Z.<lobbs sha7>-meshtastic-v<upstream version>.<upstream sha7>` | `lobbs-v2.1.0.abc1234-meshtastic-v2.7.15.567b8ea` |
| `lobbs-meshcore-firmware` | `lobbs-vX.Y.Z.<lobbs sha7>-meshcore-v<upstream version>.<upstream sha7>` | `lobbs-v2.1.0.abc1234-meshcore-v1.9.1.def5678` |

- `<lobbs sha7>` is the plugin commit the fork pins (the `vX.Y.Z` tag's commit).
- `<upstream version>.<upstream sha7>` is the upstream release and commit the fork's `lobbs` branch is based on (`git merge-base lobbs upstream/<branch>`).
- Annotated tags only (`git tag -a`).

## Release procedure

1. Plugin: update `CHANGELOG.md`, commit, `git tag -a vX.Y.Z`, push the tag.
2. Each fork: set the committed `lib_deps` pin to the `vX.Y.Z` commit sha. Confirm no `symlink://` is committed. Build a representative env from a clean clone (`seeed_solar_node` on Meshtastic).
3. Commit the pin bump, tag with the fork format above, push branch and tag.
